.TH MAY 1 "2026-08-20" "may 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
may \- ask a human before one exact action
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B may
.RI [ JOB ]
.br
.B may pending
.br
.B may request
.I JOB
.br
.B may decide
.I DIGEST
.br
.B may
.RB { check | help | version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B may
reads one human-readable action from standard input (stdin) and binds a human
answer to those exact bytes.
The action must be non-empty UTF-8 without NUL and may contain at most 16 KiB.
.PP
Without
.IR JOB ,
May writes the quoted action and its digest to
.B /dev/tty
and asks y/N there.
Only y or yes, case-insensitively, approves.
Standard input is never an approval channel.
.PP
With
.IR JOB ,
May computes lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 over the exact byte sequence
.BR may-v1 ,
NUL, the job, NUL, and the exact action. This is the public v1 digest wire
contract.
A matching grant is atomically moved to spent state before status 0.
A matching decline returns status 3.
With neither, May records a pending request and returns status 75.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "request " JOB
Perform the same exact job transition and write one strict JSON result with
the version, job, digest, action, and parked, declined, or spent verdict.
The exit status remains 75, 3, or 0; state or output failure is status 2.
This command reports authority and never creates it.
.TP
.B pending
Write every validated pending request as one JSON object per line.
.TP
.BI "decide " DIGEST
Load one pending request, display its job, quoted action, and digest on the
controlling terminal, and ask y/N.
Approval moves it to granted state; refusal moves it to declined state.
.TP
.B check
Run the offline acceptance check in a temporary state directory.
.TP
.BR help , " " \-h , " " \--help
Print a command summary.
.TP
.BR version , " " \-V , " " \--version
Print the May version.
.TP
.B \--
Treat the following single word as a job, even when it is a command name or
begins with a hyphen.
.SH STATE
State is stored under
.BR ~/.local/state/may .
The
.BR pending ,
.BR granted ,
.BR declined ,
and
.B spent
directories contain exact request records.
.B audit.jsonl
is an append-only record of times, jobs, digests, exact actions, and verdicts.
There is no state-location environment variable or configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A human approved the exact action, or a non-gating command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The acceptance check found a failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, input, state, or I/O failure.
.TP
.B 3
A human declined, or no controlling terminal was available to ask one.
.TP
.B 75
The exact job request is durably parked awaiting a human.
.SH SECURITY
May itself, its decision command, and its state are operator capabilities.
They must remain outside model toolboxes and agent-writable sandboxes.
Consequential connector programs invoke May by an absolute,
operator-controlled path.
.PP
May has no auto-approve flag, environment bypass, model judgment, daemon,
network request, or configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
printf '%s\n' 'publish release v1.4.2' | may
printf '%s\n' 'publish release v1.4.2' | may release-142
printf '%s\n' 'publish release v1.4.2' | may request release-142
may pending
may decide DIGEST
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cage (1),
.BR vouch (1)
